WEBVTT

00:05:28.755 --> 00:05:31.518
once they've earned the authority
to do things differently,

00:05:31.542 --> 00:05:32.941
and that is a trap.

00:05:33.339 --> 00:05:35.960
Because if I've learned anything
from working with Jane,

00:05:35.984 --> 00:05:37.596
it's that when that day comes,

00:05:37.620 --> 00:05:40.597
John will wonder how he could
possibly do anything differently

00:05:40.621 --> 00:05:43.727
in his high-stakes,
high-pressure executive job

00:05:43.751 --> 00:05:47.307
without risking his own success
and the organization's,

00:05:47.331 --> 00:05:51.128
and he'll wish it didn't feel
so safe and so easy

00:05:51.152 --> 00:05:54.021
to keep doing things
the way they've always been done.

00:05:55.353 --> 00:05:58.346
So the leadership development
expert in me asks:

00:05:58.370 --> 00:06:01.216
How can we better intervene
in the formative years